 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 27.8%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 3.91"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":118.43,"default_fair_val":118.43,"premium_pct":-20.7,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":67.3,"pe_forward":59.2,"pb_trailing":10.4,"pb_forward":9.4,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":9.3,"fcf_to_ev":2.89,"fcf_to_mcap":2.67,"liab_to_assets":27.8,"cash_to_assets":57.8,"current_ratio":3.91,"roe":15.4,"roa":11.1,"moat":{"ticker":"KNSA","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的品牌定價權相對穩固，主要體現在其針對特定罕見疾病的創新藥物上。這些藥物解決了未被滿足的醫療需求，使得公司能夠在市場上獲得較高的定價能力。與其他藥廠相比，Kiniksa 在其專注的細分領域具有一定的差異化優勢，但其品牌影響力尚未達到像大型製藥巨頭那樣的廣泛認知度。其商業模式依賴於持續的研發投入和臨床試驗成功，以維持其產品的獨特性和市場地位。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals possesses relatively solid brand pricing power, primarily reflected in its innovative drugs for specific rare diseases. These drugs address unmet medical needs, enabling the company to command higher pricing power in the market. Compared to other pharmaceutical companies, Kiniksa has a certain degree of differentiation advantage in its focused niche areas, but its brand influence has not yet reached the widespread recognition of major pharmaceutical giants. Its business model relies on continuous R&D investment and successful clinical trials to maintain the uniqueness and market position of its products."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的專利和監管壁壘極為強大。其核心產品受到嚴格的專利保護，為公司提供了長期的市場獨佔期。此外，藥品行業的嚴格監管審批流程本身就構成了極高的進入壁壘，新競爭者難以複製其藥品開發和獲批的歷程。這種專利和監管的雙重保護，是其商業模式的堅實基石，確保了其在特定治療領域的領先地位，並使其能夠持續獲取超額利潤。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals' patents and regulatory barriers are extremely strong. Its core products are protected by stringent patents, providing the company with a long period of market exclusivity. Furthermore, the rigorous regulatory approval process in the pharmaceutical industry itself constitutes a very high barrier to entry, making it difficult for new competitors to replicate its drug development and approval journey. This dual protection of patents and regulations is the solid cornerstone of its business model, ensuring its leading position in specific therapeutic areas and allowing it to continuously earn excess profits."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"對於 Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的患者而言，轉換至其他藥物的成本相對較高，這主要源於治療的連續性和對特定藥物的依賴性。一旦患者開始使用 Kiniksa 的藥物並產生療效，醫生和患者通常傾向於維持現有治療方案，以避免潛在的療效中斷或副作用風險。然而，這種轉換成本並非絕對，仍需考量新藥的療效、安全性及成本效益。因此，其轉換成本壁壘屬於中等偏上水平。","comment_en":"For patients of Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals, the cost of switching to other medications is relatively high, primarily due to treatment continuity and dependence on specific drugs. Once patients start using Kiniksa's drugs and achieve therapeutic effects, doctors and patients tend to maintain the existing treatment regimen to avoid potential interruptions in efficacy or risks of side effects. However, this switching cost is not absolute and still needs to consider the efficacy, safety, and cost-effectiveness of new drugs. Therefore, its switching cost barrier is at a moderate to upper level."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的業務模式主要基於單一產品的療效和專利保護，而非典型的網絡效應。其產品的價值並非隨著用戶數量的增加而顯著提升。雖然醫生和患者之間的經驗交流可能間接影響產品推廣，但這並非其核心競爭優勢。與社交媒體或平台型企業不同，Kiniksa 的網絡效應壁壘極為薄弱，其增長主要依賴於產品本身的創新和市場滲透。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals' business model is primarily based on the efficacy and patent protection of its single products, rather than typical network effects. The value of its products does not significantly increase with the growing number of users. Although the exchange of experiences among doctors and patients might indirectly influence product promotion, this is not its core competitive advantage. Unlike social media or platform-based companies, Kiniksa's network effect barrier is extremely weak; its growth relies mainly on product innovation and market penetration."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 在其特定藥物領域的規模成本優勢尚不明顯。雖然其專注於特定疾病，可能在研發和生產上具有一定的效率，但相較於大型綜合性製藥公司，其整體生產規模和採購議價能力相對較弱。其成本結構更多地受到研發投入和臨床試驗支出的影響，而非規模經濟帶來的顯著成本降低。因此，其規模成本壁壘處於中等水平。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals' cost advantage from scale in its specific drug areas is not yet apparent. Although its focus on specific diseases may lead to certain efficiencies in R&D and production, its overall production scale and purchasing power are relatively weaker compared to large, diversified pharmaceutical companies. Its cost structure is more influenced by R&D investments and clinical trial expenditures rather than significant cost reductions derived from economies of scale. Therefore, its cost advantage from scale is at a moderate level."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的業務主要集中在藥品研發和銷售，並無明顯的獨特地理位置或實物資產壁壘。其價值主要體現在知識產權和研發能力上，而非特定地區的資源或市場壟斷。雖然其產品可能在全球範圍內銷售，但這並未形成基於地理位置的獨特競爭優勢。因此，此維度的護城河評分較低。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals' business is primarily focused on drug R&D and sales, with no obvious unique geographical location or tangible asset barriers. Its value is mainly reflected in intellectual property and R&D capabilities, rather than resources or market monopolies in specific regions. Although its products may be sold globally, this does not form a unique competitive advantage based on geographical location. Therefore, the moat score for this dimension is low."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 在其營運效率方面表現出色，尤其體現在其專注於罕見病藥物的研發和商業化能力上。公司能夠高效地推進臨床試驗，並成功將創新藥物推向市場，這顯示了其卓越的營運管理和執行力。高 ROE (15.4%) 和 ROA (11.1%) 以及強勁的自由現金流 (FCF TTM: $197.2M) 均佐證了其營運效率。其精簡的組織架構和對核心業務的專注，有助於維持高水平的營運效率。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals demonstrates excellent operational efficiency, particularly in its ability to develop and commercialize rare disease drugs. The company can efficiently advance clinical trials and successfully bring innovative drugs to market, showcasing its outstanding operational management and execution. High ROE (15.4%) and ROA (11.1%), along with strong Free Cash Flow (FCF TTM: $197.2M), all attest to its operational efficiency. Its streamlined organizational structure and focus on core business contribute to maintaining a high level of operational efficiency."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的資本配置策略似乎聚焦於內部研發和潛在的戰略性收購，以擴充其產品線和治療領域。公司擁有健康的現金儲備 ($568.8M) 和極低的負債 ($7.9M)，這為其提供了充足的財務靈活性來支持研發投入和未來增長。其高 ROE 和 ROA 表明其資本配置能夠產生良好的回報。然而，作為一家仍在成長階段的公司，其長期資本配置的有效性仍需持續觀察。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals' capital allocation strategy appears to focus on internal R&D and potential strategic acquisitions to expand its product pipeline and therapeutic areas. The company possesses healthy cash reserves ($568.8M) and very low debt ($7.9M), providing it with ample financial flexibility to support R&D investments and future growth. Its high ROE and ROA indicate that its capital allocation is generating good returns. However, as a company still in its growth phase, the long-term effectiveness of its capital allocation needs continuous observation."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的客戶留存率主要體現在患者對其藥物的依賴性上，這與其藥物的療效和治療的連續性密切相關。一旦患者對其藥物產生良好的反應，且無明顯副作用，醫生和患者通常會傾向於長期使用。然而，這種留存並非完全由品牌忠誠度驅動，更多是基於臨床療效和缺乏更優替代品的現狀。因此，其客戶留存壁壘屬於中等水平，易受新藥研發的影響。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals' customer retention is primarily reflected in patient dependence on its drugs, which is closely related to the efficacy of its medications and treatment continuity. Once patients respond well to its drugs without significant side effects, doctors and patients tend to use them long-term. However, this retention is not entirely driven by brand loyalty but is more based on clinical efficacy and the current lack of superior alternatives. Therefore, its customer retention barrier is at a moderate level and can be influenced by new drug development."},"m10_durability":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 的業務具有較強的持久性，這主要歸功於其專注於罕見疾病領域的創新藥物。這些藥物往往具有較長的生命週期和穩定的市場需求，且受到嚴格的專利保護。儘管面臨新藥研發的挑戰和潛在的競爭，但其核心產品的獨特性和未被滿足的醫療需求，為其業務的長期穩定性提供了保障。強勁的財務狀況和持續的研發投入也支持了其業務的持久性。","comment_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals' business possesses strong durability, primarily attributed to its focus on innovative drugs for rare diseases. These drugs often have long lifecycles and stable market demand, and are protected by stringent patents. Despite challenges from new drug development and potential competition, the uniqueness of its core products and the unmet medical needs provide a guarantee for the long-term stability of its business. Its strong financial position and continuous R&D investment also support the durability of its business."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals 展現出一個典型的「專利型」或「收費橋型」的經濟護城河。其最強的壁壘來自於藥品專利和嚴格的監管審批，這為其創新藥物提供了長期的市場獨佔權，並構成了極高的行業進入門檻。公司在特定罕見病治療領域的營運效率和研發能力亦相當突出，能夠持續產生穩定的現金流和良好的股東回報。雖然其品牌影響力和網絡效應相對薄弱，但核心產品的臨床療效和患者依賴性提供了中等水平的客戶留存和轉換成本壁壘。整體而言，Kiniksa 憑藉其專利和監管優勢，在特定醫療領域築起了堅固的護城河。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals exhibits a typical 'patent-driven' or 'toll bridge' economic moat. Its strongest barriers stem from drug patents and rigorous regulatory approvals, which grant its innovative drugs long-term market exclusivity and create extremely high industry entry barriers. The company's operational efficiency and R&D capabilities in specific rare disease therapeutic areas are also quite outstanding, enabling it to consistently generate stable cash flow and good shareholder returns. Although its brand influence and network effects are relatively weak, the clinical efficacy of its core products and patient dependence provide moderate barriers in customer retention and switching costs. Overall, Kiniksa has built a solid moat in its specific healthcare niche, leveraging its patent and regulatory advantages.","evidenceHash":"c84d2b959309e9ca69c107715e21691ffdcc27fa6612d8209906ad19d2be38da","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"c84d2b959309e9ca69c107715e21691ffdcc27fa6612d8209906ad19d2be38da","currentEvidenceHash":"c84d2b959309e9ca69c107715e21691ffdcc27fa6612d8209906ad19d2be38da"},"fScore":{"score":9,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T03:05:40.512Z","evidenceHash":"4747b591bb040e247ada3d66456980c4a93e21b631cb2212b03dd611496d91a7"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"highRisk","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T03:05:40.512Z","evidenceHash":"4747b591bb040e247ada3d66456980c4a93e21b631cb2212b03dd611496d91a7"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/KNSA.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/KNSA.png","website":"https://www.kiniksa.com","ceo":"Sanj K. Patel","full_time_employees":"366","description":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc, a biopharmaceutical company, develops and commercializes medical therapies in the United States, the United Kingdom, and internationally. The company offers ARCALYST, an interleukin-1alpha and 1beta cytokine trap for the treatment of recurrent pericarditis, a chronic autoinflammatory cardiovascular disease and cardiac sarcoidosis. It also develops KPL-387, an investigational and fully human immunoglobulin G2 monoclonal antibody, which is Phase 2/3 clinical trial for the treatment of recurrent pericarditis; and KPL-116, a Fc-modified immunoglobulin G2 monoclonal antibody, which is in pre-clinical stage. The company was formerly known as Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals, Ltd. and changed its name to Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc in June 2024. Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc was incorporated in 2015 and is based in London, the United Kingdom.","description_en":"Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc, a biopharmaceutical company, develops and commercializes medical therapies in the United States, the United Kingdom, and internationally. The company offers ARCALYST, an interleukin-1alpha and 1beta cytokine trap for the treatment of recurrent pericarditis, a chronic autoinflammatory cardiovascular disease and cardiac sarcoidosis. It also develops KPL-387, an investigational and fully human immunoglobulin G2 monoclonal antibody, which is Phase 2/3 clinical trial for the treatment of recurrent pericarditis; and KPL-116, a Fc-modified immunoglobulin G2 monoclonal antibody, which is in pre-clinical stage. The company was formerly known as Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals, Ltd. and changed its name to Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc in June 2024. Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc was incorporated in 2015 and is based in London, the United Kingdom.","description_zh":"**Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc (KNSA) 業務營運分析**\n\nKiniksa Pharmaceuticals International, plc 是一家專注於開發與商業化醫療療法之生技製藥公司，業務範圍涵蓋美國、英國及國際市場。\n\n該公司核心產品為 **ARCALYST**，此為一種針對復發性心包炎（一種慢性自體發炎性心血管疾病）及心臟肉芽腫病所設計的介白素-1α（IL-1α）及介白素-1β（IL-1β）細胞激素捕捉劑。\n\n研發管線方面，Kiniksa 正積極推進 **KPL-387**，這是一款處於第二/三期臨床試驗階段的實驗性全人源化 IgG2 單株抗體，同樣用於治療復發性心包炎。此外，公司亦有處於臨床前階段的 **KPL-116**，此為一款經 Fc 結構修飾的 IgG2 單株抗體。\n\nKiniksa 的營運模式聚焦於透過其專有技術平台，開發針對未獲滿足醫療需求的自體發炎性疾病之創新療法，並透過臨床開發、法規審批及商業化，將其產品推向市場。公司成立於 2015 年，原名 Kiniksa Pharmaceuticals, Ltd.，並於 2024 年 6 月更名為現名，總部位於英國倫敦。","address":"105 Piccadilly","city":"London","state":"GL","zip":"W1J 7NJ","country":"GB","phone":"7814399100","full_addre